            <ArticleTitle>A case of torsion of a mucinous cystadenoma in triple-X syndrome with pure gonadal dysgenesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Triple-X female characterized by primary amenorrhea and pure gonadal dysgenesis is extremely rare. We present a patient of triple-X syndrome who has not had menarche or the development of the secondary sexual characteristics. She had a hypoplastic uterus and streaked gonads on both sides with a twisted mucinous cystadenoma in the right adnexa.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
